# Partita No. 5 in G major, BWV 829: Passepied (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: the sixth movement, a passepied: a quick, light Breton
# dance in 3/8, one beat to the bar. Here it is a three-part texture
# with a singing top line (mordents and little thirty-second turns), an
# inner voice in tied eighths and a bass that runs into sixteenths in
# the second half. Gay and springing, never driven.
#
# Time signature: 3/8 with an eighth-note upbeat; 48 bars. Two halves,
# each repeated: A from the upbeat to bar 16 (which ends with the
# upbeat to B), B bars 17-48 (Mutopia 56title-hub.mid / 56hub.ly, "6.
# Passepied"). The MIDI plays each half once; the repeats are written
# out below.
#
# Bars as performed (play, starting from the upbeat at 0.6667):
#   A first time  0.67-16.67   A repeat  16.67-32.67
#   B first time 32.67-64.67   B repeat 64.67-96.67
#   Score bar x of A is x+16 in the repeat; score bar x of B (17-48)
#   is x+16 the first time and x+48 the repeat.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 56 (eighth = 168), with both repeats about
# 1:45. Confirmed track times: Angela Hewitt (2018 recording, AHCD030,
# her own listing) 1:57; Andras Schiff (live, Amazon listing) 1:31. With
# the repeats (96 bars; without them both would be impossibly slow)
# these are about dotted quarter = 49 (Hewitt) and 63 (Schiff). 56 is
# between them: one in a bar, lively; the thirty-second turns are 5
# frames each, the fastest notes the chip can still separate.
#
# Structure (my reading of the score):
#   1-8    the tune in G major, cadence in G at 8.
#   9-16   the tune again, turning to D major; cadence in D at 16.
#   17-20  D major to E minor.
#   21-24  the top in short sighs over a running sixteenth bass on E,
#          D, C, B (A minor / C major).
#   25-28  cadence back toward G.
#   29-31  the tune's head returns in G (mordent figure, as bar 1).
#   32-36  the top in repeated sixteenth figures, A minor.
#   37-40  over the bass's sixteenths, back toward G.
#   41-48  closing phrase, final cadence in G.
#
# Plan: each half full the first time and echoed on the second manual
# for the repeat. In the B repeat the full sound returns where the
# tune's head comes back in G (score 29, performed 77), to close.

pickup 8
tempo 56 4.
play 0.6667-16.6667 0.6667-16.6667 16.6667-48.6667 16.6667-48

dyn 1 mf              # A, first time
dyn 16.6667 mp        # A repeat, from its upbeat: echo
broaden 31-32 0.95    # end of the A repeat, the D major cadence, before B
dyn 32.6667 mf        # B, first time, from its upbeat
dyn 64.6667 mp        # B repeat, echo
dyn 77 mf             # score 29 in the repeat: the tune returns in G

rit 3 0.8             # performed 94-96: the final cadence
